   "in_scope": true,
   "out_of_scope_reason": null,
   "unmapped": [
    "Multi-agent mechanism design: mechanism chooses an outcome in a finite set Omega mapping to per-agent allocations in a finite set S; welfare = seller value + sum of agent values; each agent reports a (possibly misreported) sigma-sub-Gaussian reward with mean v_i(s) in [0,1]",
    "Mechanism also sets prices; regrets measured relative to the VCG mechanism (welfare, agent, seller, and VCG regret max(n R_T, R_a, R_mech)); truthfulness and individual rationality guarantees",
    "Agents may alternatively participate by submitting bids once",
    "Learner knows the seller value function, the allocation set size |S| and the exploration length K"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "On round $t$, the  mechanism chooses an outcome $\\alloct\\in\\Alloc$ and sets prices $\\{\\priceit\\}_{i=1}^n$ for the agents. Then, agent $i$ realises a stochastic reward $\\Xit$ which has expectation $\\vali(\\alloct)$. At the end of the round, she reports a reward $\\Yit$; if she is being truthful, she would report $\\Yit=\\Xit$, but she may also choose to misreport the reward."
  },
